     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Anu made triangles from matchsticks, adding two sticks for each new triangle.\n\"How many for 10 triangles?\" asked her friend."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "pattern",
     "equation",
     "unknown"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Matchstick patterns give rules. A row of n triangles needs 2n plus 1 sticks: 3, 5, 7, 9 and so on. For 10 triangles we need 21 sticks.\nTo find how many triangles can be made with 31 sticks, solve 2n plus 1 equals 31, so 2n is 30 and n is 15.\nA frame equation puts a box where the unknown goes: box plus 7 equals 12 gives box equals 5."
    }
